    "body": "**Related Issues**\n\n - [cmd/compile: ARM64 CSE flags generation between \\`CMP 0$\\` and instruction already setting the flags according to the result #74878](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74878) <!-- score=0.86192 -->\n - [cmd/compile: inefficient compilation of (64 - x) #20677 (closed)](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/20677) <!-- score=0.84864 -->\n - [cmd/compile: optimize comparisons to min/max (u)ints by checking for overflow #41664 (closed)](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/41664) <!-- score=0.84709 -->\n - [cmd/compile/ssa: conditional select instructions #21391 (closed)](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/21391) <!-- score=0.83690 -->\n - [cmd/compile: use better code for slicing #17638](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/17638) <!-- score=0.83265 -->\n - [cmd/compile: optimize range comparisons like 'A' \\<= c \\&\\& c \\<= 'Z' #17372 (closed)](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/17372) <!-- score=0.83257 -->\n - [cmd/compile: teach prove that x \u2208 \\[0, c) \u21d2 c - x \u2208 \\[0, c) #29477 (closed)](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/29477) <!-- score=0.83194 -->\n - [cmd/compile: amd64 carry flag spilling uses SBBQ + NEGQ instead of SETCS #68961](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/68961) <!-- score=0.82956 -->\n - [cmd/compile: emit (MAX|MIN)SD instead of UCOMISD when possible #31272 (closed)](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/31272) <!-- score=0.82637 -->\n - [cmd/compile: Optimise branches that could be behind other branches, to avoid running those branches when known to be false #46711](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/46711) <!-- score=0.82526 -->\n\n<sub>(Emoji vote if this was helpful or unhelpful; more detailed feedback welcome in [this discussion](https://github.com/golang/go/discussions/67901).)</sub>\n",
