    "body": "I havn't yet finished what I wanted to do on this issue.\nUnlike `bits.Sub64` `bits.Sub32` is not intrinsicified, and it implements the 32bits overflow behavior using `uint64` in pure-go code.\nWhich often lead to suboptimal assembly generation.\n\nMy other observation is that prove gets confused by the pure-go implementation, for example in the first one it does not realize that the carry can only be 0 or 1. Fixing this and adding a couple more rules in prove to help `bits.Add32` & `bits.Sub32` might solve this issue without an intrinsic.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
