    "updated_at": "2025-11-02T14:22:38Z",
    "body": "Switching from Sub32 to Sub is not a problem in this case, because in the underflow case I return `diff + q` anyway.\n\nHowever, I am still getting the IMUL3Q with the intrinsified bits.Sub (which is an alias of bits.Sub64), which I think is unexpected after [CL 715044](https://go.dev/cl/715044)?\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
