    "updated_at": "2025-11-02T13:48:13Z",
    "body": "It is expected, `prove` only knows about a very small subset of the `bits.*` intrinsics:\nhttps://github.com/golang/go/blob/385dc33250336081c0c630938c3efede481eff76/src/cmd/compile/internal/ssa/prove.go#L1792-L1796\n\nThus it doesn't remove the `Mul` op since it doesn't know anything about the operand (except it's size).\n\nI want to systematically go through all of them and teach prove about them.\nSadly my time machine broke down a couple months ago and time has became a scarce resource for me.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
