    "updated_at": "2025-11-02T13:57:32Z",
    "body": "I have a broken CL for `bits.Add64`:\nhttps://go-review.googlesource.com/c/go/+/656336\n\nAlso for some of them I wasn't sure about UB.\n`bits.Add` & `bits.Sub` only have 0 & 1 valid values for input-carries, and things could go majorly wrong if prove doesn't model input UB the same as the host.\n\nI wanted to make `bits.Add` & `bits.Sub` panic if you pass them an invalid carry.\nas well as add new functions that would use bools for caries.\n\nhttps://groups.google.com/g/golang-dev/c/FL6vDNFjJHM/m/_bF1C4tcAAAJ\nAfter this discussion I think it's more reasonable to keep the current who knows what happen behavior but have prove only learn facts about the intrinsics if it can prove the code never input UB (in your first example prove would trivially know this to be true since you use constant 0 input-carry).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
