    "updated_at": "2025-11-02T14:13:43Z",
    "body": "Ah, all that makes sense, thank you for the details and the work.\n\nTo be clear, I am not in a rush, I was just reporting what I thought was unexpected behavior. Adding `b &= 1` does indeed make the IMUL3Q go away, although surprisingly enough it make the overall benchmarks _a lot_ worse.\n\nAnyway, only assuming [0, 1] if the input is proven to be [0, 1] sounds good to me, I only ever use these with a constant input or with another's output as the input.",
